    "If p=2, then 4 divides n^4+1 for some integer n.",
    "(n^2)^2 is congruent to 0 or 1 modulo 4.",
    "It is impossible for 4 to divide n^4+1 for integer n when p=2.",
    "Thus, p is an odd prime.",
    "For integer n such that p^2 divides n^4+1, we have p divides n^4+1.",
    "p does not divide n^4-1.",
    "p divides n^8-1.",
    "By Fermat's Little Theorem, p divides n^{p-1}-1.",
    "p divides gcd(n^{p-1}-1, n^8-1) = n^{gcd(p-1,8)}-1.",
    "gcd(p-1,8) must not divide 4, or else p divides n^4-1, which is a contradiction.",
    "So gcd(p-1,8)=8.",
    "8 divides p-1.",
    "The smallest such prime is p=17.",
    "We have to find the smallest positive integer m such that 17 divides m^4+1.",
    "A table is constructed to find m modulo 17 such that m^4+1 ≡ 0 mod 17.",
    "m ≡ ±2, ±8 mod 17.",
    "If m ≡ 2 mod 17, let m=17k+2.",
    "By the binomial theorem, (17k+2)^4+1 ≡ 17(1+32k) mod 17^2.",
    "0 ≡ 1+32k ≡ 1-2k mod 17.",
    "The smallest possible k=9, so m=155.",
    "If m ≡ -2 mod 17, let m=17k-2.",
    "By the binomial theorem, (17k-2)^4+1 ≡ 17(1-32k) mod 17^2.",
    "0 ≡ 1-32k ≡ 1+2k mod 17.",
    "The smallest possible k=8, so m=134.",
    "If m ≡ 8 mod 17, let m=17k+8.",
    "By the binomial theorem, (17k+8)^4+1 ≡ 17(241+2048k) mod 17^2.",
    "0 ≡ 241+2048k ≡ 3+8k mod 17.",
    "The smallest possible k=6, so m=110.",
    "If m ≡ -8 mod 17, let m=17k-8.",
    "By the binomial theorem, (17k-8)^4+1 ≡ 17(241-2048k) mod 17^2.",
    "0 ≡ 241+2048k ≡ 3+9k mod 17.",
    "The smallest possible k=11, so m=179.",
    "In conclusion, the smallest possible m is 110.",
    "We work in the ring Z/289Z and use the formula: fourth root of -1 is ±sqrt(1/2) ± sqrt(-1/2).",
    "-1/2 = 144 in this ring.",
    "The expression becomes ±12 ± 12i.",
    "It is calculated via Hensel that i=38, thus giving an answer of 110.",
    "n^4 + 1 ≡ 0 mod p means ord_p(n) = 8 divides p-1.",
    "The smallest prime that does this is 17 and 2^4 + 1 = 17.",
    "Let g be a primitive root of 17^2.",
    "The satisfying n are of the form g^{p(p-1)/8}, g^{3p(p-1)/8}, g^{5p(p-1)/8}, g^{7p(p-1)/8}.",
    "If we find one such n, then all n are n, n^3, n^5, n^7.",
    "2 from before is considered.",
    "17^2 divides 2^{4*17} + 1 by LTE.",
    "The possible n are 2^{17}, 2^{51}, 2^{85}, 2^{119}.",
    "2^{51} ≡ 110 is the least value."
